  "he:Bedtime Shema:3": {
   "kind": "note",
   "en": "If one did not recite Shema at its proper time in the synagogue, he must recite the two paragraphs of Shema and VeHayah Im Shamoa on his bed. The paragraph of Vayomer (tzitzit) need not be repeated if already recited in the synagogue. If one recited Shema at its proper time, only the first paragraph is needed on the bed. The Riva writes, based on Midrash, to recite all three paragraphs on the bed, as they correspond to the 248 limbs. (Devarim Hayim and Mishnah Berurah)",
   "cite": "דה\"ח ומ\"א"
  },
