 "en": {
  "en:Kiddush Levanah:6": {
   "he": [
    "he:Kiddush Levanah:6"
   ]
  },
  "en:Bedtime Shema:1": {
   "he": [
    "he:Bedtime Shema:1"
   ]
  },
  "en:Bedtime Shema:2": {
   "parts": [
    {
     "text": "Blessed are You,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " Adonoy,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " our God,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " King of the Universe,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " Who causes the fetters of sleep to fall upon my eyes,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " and slumber upon my eyelids. And illuminates the pupil of the eye. May it be Your will,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " Adonoy,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " my God and God of my fathers to make me lie down in peace,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " and to raise me (again) to good life and peace,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " and grant me my portion in Your Torah,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " make us accustomed to do Your commands,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " and let us not become accustomed to sin,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " Do not bring us into the grasp of sin,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " Do not cause us to be tested,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " or brought to disgrace. May I be ruled by the Good Inclination and let me not be ruled over by the Evil Inclination. Protect me from Satan,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " from an evil mishap and from illnesses. Let my thoughts not terrify me— nor evil dreams or evil fancies (disturb me),",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " and may my bed be perfect before You.<sup class=\"footnote-marker\">1</sup>",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": "<i class=\"footnote\">The word “bed” is used here figuratively for one’s future generations. See Rashi to Genesis 47:31; It was said of our forefather Jacob that “his bed was perfect: indicating that all his offspring were pure and steadfast.—<i>Iyun T’filoh</i>",
     "kind": "instruction"
    },
    {
     "text": "</i> And light up my eyes lest I sleep the sleep of death,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " Blessed are You,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " Adonoy,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " Who illuminates the whole world with His glory.",
     "kind": "prayer"
    }
   ],
   "he": [
    "he:Bedtime Shema:2"
   ]
  },
  "en:Bedtime Shema:3": {
   "he": [
    "he:Bedtime Shema:3"
   ]
  },
  "en:Bedtime Shema:4": {
   "he": [
    "he:Bedtime Shema:4"
   ]
  },
  "en:Bedtime Shema:5": {
   "he": [
    "he:Bedtime Shema:5"
   ]
  },
  "en:Bedtime Shema:6": {
   "he": [
    "he:Bedtime Shema:6"
   ]
  },
  "en:Bedtime Shema:7": {
   "he": [
    "he:Bedtime Shema:7"
   ]
  },
  "en:Bedtime Shema:8": {
   "parts": [
    {
     "text": "And you shall love Adonoy,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " your God with all your heart and with all your soul and with all your possessions. And these words which I command you today shall be upon your heart. And you shall teach them sharply to your children,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " and you shall discuss them when you sit in your house,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " and when you travel on the road,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " and when you lie down and when you rise. And you shall bind them for a sign upon your hand,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " and they shall be for ",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": "<i>totafos</i>",
     "kind": "instruction"
    },
    {
     "text": " between your eyes. And you shall write them upon the doorposts of your house and upon your gateways.",
     "kind": "prayer"
    }
   ],
   "he": [
    "he:Bedtime Shema:8"
   ]
  },
  "en:Bedtime Shema:9": {
   "parts": [
    {
     "text": "May the pleasantness of my Master,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " our God,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " be upon us,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": "<sup class=\"footnote-marker\">2</sup>",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": "<i class=\"footnote\">In this closing sentence of Psalm 90, Moses prays that the Divine Presence rest on the Jewish nation exclusively.</i>",
     "kind": "instruction"
    },
    {
     "text": " and the work<sup class=\"footnote-marker\">3</sup>",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": "<i class=\"footnote\">David prays first that the service Jewry performs in the Sanctuary, the sacrificial offerings, and the general performance of <i>mitzvos</i>",
     "kind": "instruction"
    },
    {
     "text": " be willingly accepted by God. Then he prays that even the work we do for our own needs be acceptable before Gold.—",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": "<i>Iyun T’Filoh</i>",
     "kind": "instruction"
    },
    {
     "text": "</i> of our hands establish for us and the work<sup class=\"footnote-marker\">4</sup>",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": "<i class=\"footnote\">The first mention of <i>work</i>",
     "kind": "instruction"
    },
    {
     "text": " refers to the actual endeavors of our hands,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " whereas the second mention of ",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": "<i>work</i>",
     "kind": "instruction"
    },
    {
     "text": " refers to what was achieved by our hands.—",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": "<i>Iyun Tefilloh</i>",
     "kind": "instruction"
    },
    {
     "text": "</i> of our hands may He establish.",
     "kind": "prayer"
    }
   ],
   "he": [
    "he:Bedtime Shema:9"
   ]
  },
  "en:Bedtime Shema:10": {
   "parts": [
    {
     "text": "He who dwells in the shelter of the Supreme One,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " under the protection of Shadai He will abide. I say of Adonoy,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " [He is] my refuge and my stronghold,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " my God in Whom I trust. For He will save you from the snare-trap,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " from destructive pestilence. With His wings He will cover you and beneath His wings,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " you will find refuge;",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " His truth is a shield,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " a full shield. You will not fear the terror of night,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " nor the arrow that flies by day,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " the pestilence that prowls in darkness,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " nor the deadly plague that ravages at noon. A thousand will fall at your [left] side,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " and ten thousand at your [right] side but it<sup class=\"footnote-marker\">5</sup>",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": "<i class=\"footnote\">“It” refers to “arrow,” “pestilence,” and “plague” of the previous verse.</i>",
     "kind": "instruction"
    },
    {
     "text": " shall not come near you. Only with your eyes will you behold and see the punishment of the wicked.<sup class=\"footnote-marker\">6</sup>",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": "<i class=\"footnote\">You will only <i>see</i>",
     "kind": "instruction"
    },
    {
     "text": " the destruction but you will not be harmed by it.</i> For you [have proclaimed]: Adonoy is my refuge,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " the Supreme One you have made your dwelling No evil shall befall you,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " and no plague shall come near your tent. For His angels He will command on your behalf— to guard you in all your ways. They will carry you upon their hands,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " lest you hurt your foot on a rock. You will tread upon lion and snake,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " you will trample young lion and serpent. Because he clings to Me with desire,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " I will save him;",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " I will strengthen him,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " for he knows My Name. When he calls upon Me,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " I will answer him;",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " I am with him in distress,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " I will free him and honor him. I will satiate him with longevity,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " and will let him see My deliverance. I will satiate him with longevity and will let him see My deliverance.",
     "kind": "prayer"
    }
   ],
   "he": [
    "he:Bedtime Shema:10"
   ]
  },
  "en:Bedtime Shema:11": {
   "parts": [
    {
     "text": "(Psalms 3:2-9) Adonoy,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " how many are my tormentors;",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": "<sup class=\"footnote-marker\">7</sup>",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": "<i class=\"footnote\">Psalm 3 was sung by David when, at the age of 65, he had to flee his son Absalom.</i>",
     "kind": "instruction"
    },
    {
     "text": " many rise up against me. Many say of my soul: There is no deliverance for him through God,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " forever. But You,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " Adonoy,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " are a shield for me;",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " my glory and Raiser of my head. With my voice,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " I call out to Adonoy,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " and He answers me from His holy mountain,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " forever. I lay down and slept;",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " I awake for Adonoy supports me. I fear not the tens of thousands of people deployed against me from every side. Rise Adonoy,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " deliver me,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " my God,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " for You have struck all my enemies<sup class=\"footnote-marker\">8</sup>",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": "<i class=\"footnote\">David is confident of God’s help, because God has always smitten his enemies.—<i>Radak</i>",
     "kind": "instruction"
    },
    {
     "text": "</i> on the cheek;",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " You have broken the teeth of the wicked. Deliverance is Adonoy's;",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " upon Your people is Your blessing, ",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": "<i>selah.</i>",
     "kind": "instruction"
    }
   ],
   "he": [
    "he:Bedtime Shema:11"
   ]
  },
  "en:Bedtime Shema:12": {
   "he": [
    "he:Bedtime Shema:12"
   ]
  },
  "en:Bedtime Shema:13": {
   "he": [
    "he:Bedtime Shema:13"
   ]
  },
  "en:Bedtime Shema:14": {
   "he": [
    "he:Bedtime Shema:14"
   ]
  },
  "en:Bedtime Shema:15": {
   "parts": [
    {
     "text": "The angel who redeemed me from all evil<sup class=\"footnote-marker\">9</sup>",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": "<i class=\"footnote\">These are the words used by Jacob when he blessed Joseph, and his sons Ephraim and Menashe.—Genesis 48:16</i>",
     "kind": "instruction"
    },
    {
     "text": " May he bless the lads;",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " and may they be called by my name and the names of my fathers,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " Abraham and Isaac;",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " and may they multiply like fish within the land.",
     "kind": "prayer"
    }
   ],
   "he": [
    "he:Bedtime Shema:15"
   ]
  },
  "en:Bedtime Shema:16": {
   "parts": [
    {
     "text": "And He said,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " \"If you will diligently heed the voice of Adonoy,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " your God,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " and do what is upright in His eyes,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " and listen carefully to His commandments,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " and guard all His statutes— [then] every sickness that I put in Egypt,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " I will not put upon you,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " for I am Adonoy,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " your Healer.<sup class=\"footnote-marker\">10</sup>",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": "<i class=\"footnote\">Exodus 15:26</i>",
     "kind": "instruction"
    }
   ],
   "he": [
    "he:Bedtime Shema:16"
   ]
  },
  "en:Bedtime Shema:17": {
   "parts": [
    {
     "text": "And Adonoy said to Satan: Adonoy rebukes you,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " Satan,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " Adonoy rebukes you,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " He Who chose Jerusalem;",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " for is this one not a firebrand plucked out of the fire?<sup class=\"footnote-marker\">11</sup>",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": "<i class=\"footnote\">Zechariah 3:2</i>",
     "kind": "instruction"
    }
   ],
   "he": [
    "he:Bedtime Shema:17"
   ]
  },
  "en:Bedtime Shema:18": {
   "parts": [
    {
     "text": "Behold the bed of Solomon! Sixty mighty men [are set] around it,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " of the mighty men of Israel. All of them armed with swords,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " trained in warfare;",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " each man has his sword at his side,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " because of the dread of the night.<sup class=\"footnote-marker\">12</sup>",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": "<i class=\"footnote\">Song of Songs 3:7-8</i>",
     "kind": "instruction"
    }
   ],
   "he": [
    "he:Bedtime Shema:18"
   ]
  },
  "en:Bedtime Shema:19": {
   "he": [
    "he:Bedtime Shema:19"
   ]
  },
  "en:Bedtime Shema:20": {
   "parts": [
    {
     "text": "Adonoy bless you and guard you! Adonoy shine His countenance upon you and be gracious unto You! Adonoy turn His countenance toward you and grant you peace!<sup class=\"footnote-marker\">13</sup>",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": "<i class=\"footnote\">Numbers 6:24-26</i>",
     "kind": "instruction"
    }
   ],
   "he": [
    "he:Bedtime Shema:20"
   ]
  },
  "en:Bedtime Shema:21": {
   "parts": [
    {
     "text": "Behold,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " He neither slumbers nor sleeps! the Guardian of Israel.<sup class=\"footnote-marker\">14</sup>",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": "<i class=\"footnote\">Psalms 121:4</i>",
     "kind": "instruction"
    }
   ],
   "he": [
    "he:Bedtime Shema:21"
   ]
  },
  "en:Bedtime Shema:22": {
   "parts": [
    {
     "text": "For your deliverance,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " I hope,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " Adonoy;",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": "<sup class=\"footnote-marker\">15</sup>",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": "<i class=\"footnote\">Genesis 49:18</i>",
     "kind": "instruction"
    },
    {
     "text": " I hope,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " Adonoy,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " for Your deliverance;",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " Adonoy,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " for Your deliverance I hope.",
     "kind": "prayer"
    }
   ],
   "he": [
    "he:Bedtime Shema:22"
   ]
  },
  "en:Bedtime Shema:23": {
   "he": [
    "he:Bedtime Shema:23"
   ]
  },
  "en:Bedtime Shema:24": {
   "parts": [
    {
     "text": "A song of ascents Fortunate are all who fear Adonoy,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " who walk in His ways. When you eat of the toil of your hands you are fortunate and it is good with you. Your wife will be like a fruitful vine in the innermost parts of your house;",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " your children like olive plants around your table. Behold! thus shall be blessed the man who fears Adonoy. Adonoy bless you from Zion! and [may you] see the good of Jerusalem all the days of your life! May you [live to] see your children's children! Peace upon Israel!<sup class=\"footnote-marker\">16</sup>",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": "<i class=\"footnote\">Psalms 128</i>",
     "kind": "instruction"
    }
   ],
   "he": [
    "he:Bedtime Shema:24"
   ]
  },
  "en:Bedtime Shema:25": {
   "he": [
    "he:Bedtime Shema:25"
   ]
  },
  "en:Bedtime Shema:26": {
   "parts": [
    {
     "text": "Tremble and do not sin;",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " commune with your hearts upon your bed,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " and be silent,",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": " selah!<sup class=\"footnote-marker\">17</sup>",
     "kind": "prayer"
    },
    {
     "text": "<i class=\"footnote\">Psalms 4:5</i>",
     "kind": "instruction"
    }
   ],
   "he": [
    "he:Bedtime Shema:26"
   ]
  },
  "en:Bedtime Shema:27": {
   "he": [
    "he:Bedtime Shema:27"
   ]
  },
  "en:Bedtime Shema:28": {
   "he": [
    "he:Bedtime Shema:28"
   ]
  },
  "en:Bedtime Shema:29": {
